WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.570
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.370
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.000
between Domino's in Japan and the US.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.087
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.493
In Japan, Domino's pizzas
come in three sizes.

00:00:14.493 --> 00:00:17.090
Our Domino's pizza comes in four sizes.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:20.610
George: So, this one is medium,
which is cut into 8 slices.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.350
Joe: Over here on this
end, you got the small.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.060
That's 10-inch pizza.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:29.060
And here's regular, which is
also cut into eight slices.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.318
Joe: Next up is our medium.

00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:32.610
That's a 12-inch pizza.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.700
And this one is large.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.730
This one is cut into 12 slices.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.820
Joe: Then we move to our large, 14 inches.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.030
And finally, the extra
large, which is 16 inches.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:47.514
Look at all that grease.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.250
A Domino's large plain pizza
has a 33-centimeters diameter

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.810
or an 855.3-square-centimeters area

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:04.130
and costs 2,000 yen.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.410
So breaking that down,

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:09.251
our pizza is 2.33 yen per square inch,

00:01:09.251 --> 00:01:11.360
or about 2 cents.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.810
Now take our large.
This is a 14-inch pizza,

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.170
also a 35.56-centimeter pizza.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:18.578
And it has a surface area

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:22.800
of 993.1 square centimeters.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.716
That's 1.4 cents per square inch,

00:01:25.716 --> 00:01:28.899
or 1.62 Japanese yen.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:33.010
But what gives you the
most food for your money?

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:36.360
So, here's a large plain
slice with a pan crust.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.650
And here's another with hand-tossed crust.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:42.520
Let's weigh both right
now and see which is more.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.323
So, first let's weigh pan crust.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.830
51 grams.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.220
And hand-tossed crust.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.370
It weighs 49 grams.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.990
And we will do the same.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.560
I want to note that right now in America,

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.058
you can only get the pan
Domino's in the medium size.

00:02:01.058 --> 00:02:03.950
Same exact experiment, only
I'm doing two medium pizzas.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.570
Medium pan slice, medium
hand-tossed slice.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:11.570
So, this is the hand-tossed slice,

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:12.861
and it weighs

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.936
a smidge over 75.

00:02:15.936 --> 00:02:16.986
We'll go 76.

00:02:16.986 --> 00:02:18.348
The pan.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:21.695
That goes in there too.

00:02:21.695 --> 00:02:23.570
110 grams.

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:27.250
Making the difference this amount.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.880
I'm not doing math.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.760
In Japan, we have seven
different crust options.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.640
No. 1, we have pan.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.726
And No. 2 we have hand-tossed.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.494
And No. 3, we have ultra-crispy.

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:43.360
Ooh.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.193
It's like a cracker.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.170
No. 4, we have cheese burst,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:53.910
where a string cheese is placed
around the edge of the crust

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.153
and sprinkled with consommé
Parmesan seasoning.

00:02:57.153 --> 00:02:58.480
Ooh.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.940
No. 5, we have the cheese 'n' roll.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:05.997
It's got mozzarella cheese in the crust.

00:03:05.997 --> 00:03:10.250
And No. 6, we have mille-filet.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.300
Or mill-foy.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.382
Mille-fail.

00:03:15.382 --> 00:03:18.180
In Japanese we say mi-ru fi-yu.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.300
So this one is mi-ru-fi-yu pizza,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.290
which has two layers of crust

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.891
with Camembert mixed cheese in between.

00:03:24.891 --> 00:03:26.449
Mille-fail.

00:03:26.449 --> 00:03:28.265
Mille-fee-yuh.

00:03:28.265 --> 00:03:31.320
French people, please
correct my pronunciation.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.095
No. 7, the last one we have,

00:03:34.095 --> 00:03:36.595
the triple mille-feuille.

00:03:36.595 --> 00:03:40.275
It's got three layers of
crust with cheese in between.

00:03:40.275 --> 00:03:41.133
Wow.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:43.983
In the US, we have only
five crust options.

00:03:43.983 --> 00:03:45.720
I realize there's four
pizzas in front of me.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:46.553
Let me explain.

00:03:46.553 --> 00:03:48.300
One crust option you can get here,

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.170
and it's a small only,
is the gluten-free crust.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:57.170
I don't know how bread is gluten-free,

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.492
but we figured it out.

00:03:59.492 --> 00:04:00.425
Ta-da.

00:04:00.425 --> 00:04:02.990
We also have the hand-tossed,

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:05.995
which is more of a standard pillowy,

00:04:05.995 --> 00:04:07.178
I mean, right, this is
like standard dough,

00:04:07.178 --> 00:04:08.495
this is what we think a pizza looks like.

00:04:08.495 --> 00:04:10.886
This is the pan.

00:04:10.886 --> 00:04:12.286
Look how thick that is, man.

00:04:12.286 --> 00:04:14.350
That's, like, triple the dough thickness.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:15.550
Good on you for the pan.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.860
Now, you can get this in the medium only.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.704
We also have a crunchy thin crust.

00:04:20.704 --> 00:04:22.640
And we have so many
pizzas here, to be honest,

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:23.870
I don't know which one it is.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.620
So when it just comes up in
the video, I'll show it off.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.590
But imagine a crunchy thin pizza.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.130
Oddly enough, we also
have something called

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.410
the Brooklyn-style pizza.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.090
This is reserved for large
and extra-large pizzas only.

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:37.980
And this is a Brooklyn-style
right here, extra large.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.550
Obviously it isn't crispy,
because it's sagging.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.005
This is really thin.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.282
Here's everything you can
get at the Japanese Domino's

00:04:47.282 --> 00:04:49.910
that you cannot get in the US.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.890
Here's everything you
can get at a US Domino's

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.553
you cannot get in Japan.

00:04:53.553 --> 00:04:56.020
Everyone, look at this.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.710
This is a limited-time-offer pizza.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.730
It's called the Best 34.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:02.977
Look at this lid.

00:05:02.977 --> 00:05:05.385
It's disgusting!

00:05:05.385 --> 00:05:07.872
Don't look at me! Don't look at me!

00:05:07.872 --> 00:05:11.350
So, this one has all 34 Domino's toppings,

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:15.827
like teriyaki chicken, mayo,
spinach, tomato, shrimp.

00:05:15.827 --> 00:05:17.874
This is huge.

00:05:17.874 --> 00:05:19.866
It's like my baby.

00:05:19.866 --> 00:05:23.699
[sings lullaby]

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.810
The New Yorker-style pizza is similar

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.910
to the Brooklyn XL option
you can get in America.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:33.140
But only in Japan you can
get the Quattro New Yorker.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.570
It's a 16-inch pizza with
each New Yorker topping style

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.660
covering a quarter of the pizza.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:42.440
So one quarter is pepperoni,
and one is cheese,

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.570
and one is pepperoni and sausage,

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.890
and one is ham and mushroom.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:50.080
So, here we have Nippon favorites series.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.630
Nippon, or Nihon, means Japan in Japanese.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:56.120
So these pizzas feature
Japanese ingredients.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.584
This one charcoal-grilled
teriyaki chicken.

00:05:58.584 --> 00:06:02.330
It's got teriyaki chicken, teriyaki sauce,

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:05.670
spinach, mayonnaise, and corn.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.450
Next we have Hokkaido three cheeses.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:12.230
So, Hokkaido is the northern
island prefecture in Japan,

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:14.910
and it's famous for its cheese.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.793
It's got Hokkaido Gouda cheese,

00:06:16.793 --> 00:06:18.409
Hokkaido cheddar cheese,

00:06:18.409 --> 00:06:21.560
and Hokkaido Camembert
and sliced asparagus.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.100
We have spicy mayo and mochi.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.107
It's got mochi rice cake and corn,

00:06:27.107 --> 00:06:30.081
pork sausage and sliced asparagus,

00:06:30.081 --> 00:06:31.847
and Korean seaweed flakes.

00:06:31.847 --> 00:06:34.500
And last one, we've got
charcoal-grilled beef

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.393
and spinach and mushrooms.

00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:41.124
Mm!

00:06:41.124 --> 00:06:42.557
Oh!

00:06:42.557 --> 00:06:43.848
Umai!

00:06:44.857 --> 00:06:46.560
Umai!

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.801
This beef is so tender,

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:53.800
and it's got so much,
like, charcoal flavor,

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.705
which makes this amazing.

00:06:55.705 --> 00:06:56.950
I love this.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.260
So many exclusive pizzas
here at the US Domino's.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.140
I don't know where to begin,

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.920
so I'll just start with
this one that I'm holding.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:06.400
This is the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.440
I don't know what makes it
California-in-y or Cali-y,

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:13.250
but it definitely has
chicken, and bacon, and ranch,

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.480
and it's big.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:15.570
Thank you very much.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:16.453
All right.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:18.718
Chicken taco pizza.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.880
Oh, yeah.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.470
Got taco spices to it.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.310
Good job on this one.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.114
Next one, the cheeseburger pizza.

00:07:27.114 --> 00:07:28.230
Um ...

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.223
Yeah. Oh, my God.

00:07:33.223 --> 00:07:34.640
I'm going to say something crazy.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.030
This tastes exactly like
a McDonald's cheeseburger.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:39.653
Even has the oniony
and the ketchupy taste.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.160
Wow.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:43.858
That is a surprise.

00:07:43.858 --> 00:07:44.780
I thought this one was going to be bad,

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:45.980
but it's actually pretty good.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:49.940
The extravaganZZa.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:54.290
This has pepperoni, sausage, ham,

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:58.382
mushrooms, black olives, green peppers.

00:07:58.382 --> 00:07:59.880
This is the meatZZa,

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.710
which I'm assuming is just a lot of meat.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.297
I'm seeing sausage, I'm seeing pepperoni,

00:08:05.297 --> 00:08:06.423
and maybe hamburger.

00:08:10.084 --> 00:08:11.127
Yeah, I'll put this in the good pile.

00:08:11.127 --> 00:08:11.960
I f--- with this one.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:12.980
Philly cheesesteak.

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:14.510
Oh, no.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.900
In some weird way, I'm
blaming you for this.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.780
Since you handed this to
me, this is your fault.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.370
Look at this nightmare.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.220
Meat somewhere on here.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:25.160
I'm also seeing green peppers.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:28.167
Oh. Look, look, it's like,

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:30.217
look at that, it's,
like, stuck to the box.

00:08:34.601 --> 00:08:35.950
No.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:36.910
Buffalo chicken.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.185
OK, OK.

00:08:38.185 --> 00:08:39.172
This is more my speed.

00:08:39.172 --> 00:08:40.046
Chicken.

00:08:40.046 --> 00:08:41.600
No, not tomato sauce, like a white sauce.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:42.433
Good call.

00:08:44.585 --> 00:08:46.390
Mm!

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:48.060
This isn't Buffalo enough.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.680
The capital of the great state of New York

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.013
needs to be better
represented in this pizza.

00:08:53.013 --> 00:08:56.167
The capital of New York
is Buffalo, correct?

00:08:56.167 --> 00:08:57.020
No?

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.240
We got the Memphis barbecue chicken.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.370
Love Memphis.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:01.420
Love barbecue.

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:02.423
Love chicken.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:05.770
Yeah.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.210
The key thing here is the barbecue sauce.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.840
I don't know what is in it,
but, man, that's really good.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:10.673
Memphis,

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:14.480
capital of the great state of Tennessee.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:19.480
Everyone, here is the
ultra cheese New Yorker.

00:09:19.945 --> 00:09:22.245
It's got 1 kilogram of cheese,

00:09:22.245 --> 00:09:24.695
or 2.2 pounds.

00:09:24.695 --> 00:09:27.152
OMG.

00:09:27.152 --> 00:09:27.985
Ooh!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.001
Look how thick this cheese is!

00:09:32.001 --> 00:09:32.834
Go!

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:41.320
Go home.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.740
It weighs 180 grams,

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:46.781
180 times eight equals

00:09:46.781 --> 00:09:50.206
1,440 grams in total.

00:09:50.206 --> 00:09:53.250
So, here are other
Japanese specialty pizzas.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.580
So, here we have quattro meat max.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:59.065
So it's got charcoal-grilled
teriyaki chicken

00:09:59.065 --> 00:10:01.506
and charcoal-grilled beef

00:10:01.506 --> 00:10:05.047
and giga meat and Goryeo galbi.

00:10:05.047 --> 00:10:08.000
It's Korean-style beef pizza.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.193
And next we have seafood special.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:14.510
This part and this part
is shrimp mayonnaise.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.210
So this part, it's got shrimp, octopus,

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:19.526
mussels, littleneck clams,

00:10:19.526 --> 00:10:22.034
Mactra clams, green peppers,

00:10:22.034 --> 00:10:23.620
and cherry tomatoes.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:26.828
Next we've got garlic master.

00:10:26.828 --> 00:10:28.610
Looks so spicy.

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:32.480
Garlic and pork sausage and pancetta.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.018
And this part has got jalapeño, obviously.

00:10:36.018 --> 00:10:38.018
It's picante.

00:10:38.018 --> 00:10:41.490
Pepperoni and Italian sausage and onions.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:43.860
And look at this huge thing.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.370
Mayo jaga.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:49.366
So, jaga, or jagaimo,
means potato in Japanese.

00:10:49.366 --> 00:10:51.807
It's got potato and pork sausage

00:10:51.807 --> 00:10:53.682
and a lot of mayo.

00:10:53.682 --> 00:10:56.680
Joe: Our US Domino's has
sandwiches and pasta.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.260
I was not a fan of the
Philly cheesesteak pizza,

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.240
but let's see what the Philly
cheesesteak tastes like

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:04.623
in its native form of sandwich.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:07.548
Better than the pizza.

00:11:07.548 --> 00:11:08.780
Also at the US Domino's,

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:10.540
you can get a Buffalo chicken sandwich,

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.056
a chicken habanero sandwich,

00:11:12.056 --> 00:11:13.207
the Mediterranean veggie,

00:11:13.207 --> 00:11:14.040
no, thanks,

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.290
a chicken bacon ranch,

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:16.250
an Italian sandwich,

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:19.130
and, of course, the chicken Parm sandwich.

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:21.480
Our Domino's has four
pastas to choose from.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.632
I only got two, the chicken Alfredo

00:11:23.632 --> 00:11:25.730
and the Italian sausage marinara.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:29.260
You can also get a chicken
carbonara and a pasta primavera.

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:31.285
I've just been informed
I have to eat this.

00:11:36.016 --> 00:11:38.010
Strong flavor on this.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:41.890
I would skip the pasta
at Domino's, personally.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.300
This thing is, like, baked on.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.290
See how baked this is?

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:45.380
Like, come on.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.335
I feel like chef Ramsay here.

00:11:46.335 --> 00:11:50.120
Just, "Oh, come on. Oh,
this baked on here!"

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:52.630
In the US, we have a few chicken options

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:53.780
you can't get in Japan.

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:55.271
Yes, Japan has wings,

00:11:55.271 --> 00:11:56.720
but they don't have these flavors.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:58.557
Visually, I can see why.

00:11:58.557 --> 00:12:02.630
First flavor we got here
is the garlic Parmesan.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:05.880
Hey, Domino's, what are you doing?

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.371
Next one, we got,

00:12:07.371 --> 00:12:10.340
I'm assuming this is the honey barbecue.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:12.240
These drizzles! What are you
guys doing drizzling, man?

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:13.490
Just toss it!

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:15.160
Toss it in the sauce!

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:16.423
Nobody wants a drizzle.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.272
Oh, wait a second.

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:23.447
This is the sweet mango habanero.

00:12:23.447 --> 00:12:24.726
I wasn't expecting that heat.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:27.760
Oh, man.

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:28.630
Very good.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:30.865
These are --

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:33.513
why did you do this?

00:12:33.513 --> 00:12:35.330
Why did you do this?

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:36.820
Toss it in the sauce.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:39.390
Why'd you just squirt it on
here, like, as an afterthought?

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:40.520
Honey barbecue.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:41.590
Right? Is this not nuts?

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.582
This is nuts, right, that
they did it like this.

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.070
I like the sauce.

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:51.830
So, Domino's also does their
wings in boneless flavors.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.640
They have obviously those three,

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:55.830
and you can also get these two other ones.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.100
And I see we have the
crispy bacon and tomato,

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:01.850
and this one must be the
spicy jalapeño pineapple.

00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:02.903
Whoa, what?

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:04.800
Hell yeah.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:05.970
All right.

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:06.970
Get that B-roll fast.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:10.053
There it goes!

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.118
I know.

00:13:12.118 --> 00:13:15.980
Your audible gasps are warranted.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.296
I don't know what this --

00:13:18.296 --> 00:13:20.429
what am I supposed to do with this?

00:13:20.429 --> 00:13:22.590
Ooh, this one I'm looking
forward to, Yuelei.

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:24.600
We got the food less than an hour ago.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:28.275
I don't think an hour is
unrealistic for food to sit.

00:13:28.275 --> 00:13:29.838
I think you guys gotta
put some more chemicals

00:13:29.838 --> 00:13:31.840
in your cheese to keep it goopier longer.

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.640
Ooh, I got some pineapple,
and I got some jalapeño,

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:34.515
and I got some chicken.

00:13:34.515 --> 00:13:35.393
Let's check it out.

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:39.450
Yeah.

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:42.130
Overall, everything
here tastes pretty good.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.140
Presentation, you gotta work on that.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:46.600
In Japan, we don't have boneless wings,

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:49.725
but we have Japanese fried chicken,

00:13:49.725 --> 00:13:51.366
which is called karaage.

00:13:51.366 --> 00:13:53.840
It kind of looks like
American boneless wings.

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:56.053
Ah.

00:13:56.053 --> 00:13:57.955
I love karaage.

00:13:57.955 --> 00:14:01.190
And also we have chicken nuggets.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:04.860
Both come in four, eight, and 12 pieces.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:08.320
Our Domino's has breads
and oven-baked dips.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.030
Let's review the breads first.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:11.010
Shall we?

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:11.843
Over here,

00:14:11.843 --> 00:14:15.640
we have Parmesan bread twists
and garlic bread twists.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:19.820
I know that because of their
totally twisted shapes.

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:21.740
They also have Parmesan bread bites

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:23.040
that were currently unavailable.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.358
Whoa.

00:14:26.358 --> 00:14:27.515
Uh-oh.

00:14:27.515 --> 00:14:29.180
These are very good.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.715
To Parmesan we go.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:33.993
Not as good.

00:14:33.993 --> 00:14:35.590
But still pretty good.

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:38.680
I mean, it's bread and
cheese and oil, right?

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:41.560
US Domino's also has something
called stuffed cheesy bread.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.950
You can get your stuffed
cheesy bread with either

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:47.000
spinach and feta or bacon and jalapeños.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.000
Take a wild guess which one I chose.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:53.080
[beep] Just ripping this
whole [beep] thing apart.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.710
Oh, God!

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:56.611
This thing is especially greasy.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:03.380
For whatever reason,
Domino's didn't stop there.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.463
Domino's has something called dips.

00:15:05.463 --> 00:15:06.296
[sighs]

00:15:06.296 --> 00:15:07.848
What it appears to be

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:11.210
is a giant dish of melted cheese.

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:14.250
And you can get it in cheesy
marinara or five cheese.

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.186
What are we doing, Domino's?

00:15:16.186 --> 00:15:19.070
[laughs]

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:20.680
What is this?

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:23.200
Come on, guys.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:25.230
So, this is the marinara
one, I'm assuming.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:27.680
A pizza without the bread, right?

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:31.841
These dips are literally
zapping my will to live.

00:15:31.841 --> 00:15:33.315
Please don't ever get ...

00:15:34.967 --> 00:15:38.680
It's a whole bowl of cheese, Yuelei!

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:41.613
Why would -- oh, look
at the oil in this too!

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:44.500
Everyone in here just gagged.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.958
Can I even dip it?

00:15:53.114 --> 00:15:54.780
Oh, whoa.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.690
I don't know what of the
five cheeses is in here,

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:58.563
like, which five.

00:16:00.002 --> 00:16:01.758
Why am I eating this?!

00:16:02.908 --> 00:16:04.341
Ugh!

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:09.690
So, here are our Japanese
exclusive side-menu items.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.370
Let's start with this one.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:14.800
We've got oven-baked potato wedges.

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.440
This one is plain.

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:17.940
Consommé.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:19.670
Chili garlic.

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:21.863
And this one is butter.

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:26.232
And next we have cheese sticks.

00:16:27.099 --> 00:16:28.810
Shrimp popcorn.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:33.250
It comes with this tartar sauce.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:36.120
Here we have choregi salad.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:39.495
We've got Korean-style seaweed flakes

00:16:39.495 --> 00:16:41.961
and choregi dressing.

00:16:41.961 --> 00:16:46.860
So, choregi is, like,
Korean-style sesame-oil dressing.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.363
And fresh salad in the package.

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:54.860
So, here we have corn potage.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.050
Clam chowder.

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:57.400
Minestrone.

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:59.290
Black chili.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:00.610
You've seen these before.

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:04.152
It is the Domino's
marbled cookie brownies.

00:17:04.152 --> 00:17:06.560
♪ Liquid sugar ♪

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:07.920
Oh, yeah.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.800
You can also get these
cinnamon bread twists.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.700
Lastly, another dip.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:17.200
I swear to God, if there's cheese in this,

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.292
I'm walking out of here
and I'm never coming back.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:24.230
Baked apple dips.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.520
And I'm assuming you dip these into this.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.636
I'm not gonna.

00:17:28.636 --> 00:17:30.650
So, here are our other desserts.

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.440
We have mini pancakes,

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:36.130
heart-shaped fondant chocolate,

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:39.850
and here we have egg custard tart.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:43.049
I have never tried this one before.

00:17:43.049 --> 00:17:44.199
Itadakimasu.

00:17:46.692 --> 00:17:48.279
Mm.

00:17:48.279 --> 00:17:49.810
Mm!

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:51.010
This is so good.

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:52.448
So flaky.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:55.280
Mm.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:58.158
This one is apple pie.

00:17:58.158 --> 00:18:00.943
And next we have custard pie.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:05.930
Lastly, of the sodas
you can get in the US,

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.380
can't get in Japan,

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:11.121
get yourself Fanta orange and Sprite.

00:18:11.121 --> 00:18:13.770
We have Coke Zero.

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:15.137
It's supposed to be Zero,

00:18:15.137 --> 00:18:17.636
but they gave us just normal Coke.

00:18:17.636 --> 00:18:20.311
Next, we have ginger ale.

00:18:20.311 --> 00:18:21.800
Canada Dry.

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:25.240
Canada is an amazing country, eh?

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:26.673
Qoo orange juice.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.213
And here is Sokenbicha.

00:18:30.213 --> 00:18:32.380
It's Japanese blended tea.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:36.430
And last one, we've got Georgia Japan

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:38.779
Craftsman café latte.

00:18:38.779 --> 00:18:40.380
Georgia Japan.

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:42.804
Sounds like George Japan.

00:18:42.804 --> 00:18:44.750
I'd like to be sponsored by you.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:46.230
Let me try this.

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:51.790
It's got a lot of milk and sugar in it.

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:52.902
I gotta be honest.

00:18:52.902 --> 00:18:54.402
It's not my taste.

00:18:58.341 --> 00:18:59.226
Take two.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.565
I really love this.

00:19:02.565 --> 00:19:05.161
Please give me a sponsorship.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:09.065
A Japan large hand-tossed pizza

00:19:09.065 --> 00:19:11.700
is 130 calories per slice,

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:16.290
or 1,560 calories for the full pizza.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:20.300
In the US, a large hand-tossed
pizza slice is 280 calories,

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:24.953
which makes the entire
pizza 2,240 calories.

00:19:24.953 --> 00:19:27.280
A large big-pepperoni hand-tossed slice

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:30.410
is 335 calories per slice,

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:34.220
or 4,020 calories for the entire pizza.

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:37.770
Our large pepperoni is
370 calories per slice,

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:41.834
which makes the entire pie 2,960 calories.

00:19:41.834 --> 00:19:44.284
Japan's most calorific pizza is

00:19:44.284 --> 00:19:46.900
the ultra cheese New Yorker size.

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:50.310
One slice is 478 calories.

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:54.707
That's 3,827 for the full pizza.

00:19:54.707 --> 00:19:55.920
Ah.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.270
Our US Domino's pizza
with the most calories

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:01.250
is the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:03.158
This is an XL of said pizza.

00:20:03.158 --> 00:20:05.774
One slice is 560 calories,

00:20:05.774 --> 00:20:10.650
and that makes the full
pie 3,360 calories.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:15.500
Our large plain pizza
has 1,620 calories total.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:18.460
Our large cheese is 2,240 calories.

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:21.520
That's a 38.2% increase.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:26.033
Our large big pepperoni is 2,680 calories,

00:20:26.033 --> 00:20:29.818
over 34% of your daily
recommended calorie intake.

00:20:29.818 --> 00:20:33.682
333% of your daily sodium.

00:20:33.682 --> 00:20:35.132
Ah!

00:20:35.132 --> 00:20:37.730
Too many tasty calories!

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:39.870
Ours is 2,960 calories,

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:44.270
48% over your daily recommended amount,

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:46.680
but somehow ours has less sodium,

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:50.571
only 299% of your daily sodium.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:53.828
In October of last year,

00:20:53.828 --> 00:20:57.103
a study found detectable
amounts of phthalate,

00:20:57.103 --> 00:20:59.260
a plastic softener, in common menu items

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:02.383
from large fast-food
chains, including Domino's.

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:08.038
The study analyzed 64 food samples

00:21:08.038 --> 00:21:09.988
from several popular fast-food chains

00:21:09.988 --> 00:21:14.930
and found phthalates DnBP and DEHP

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:17.010
in a majority of the items.

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:19.560
USA Today reported that,
"Food containing meat,

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:21.450
such as chicken burritos
and cheeseburgers,

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:23.770
had higher levels of
the chemicals studied,

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:26.070
while cheese pizza had the lowest levels."

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:28.430
OK, so that's good news
for Domino's, I guess.

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:31.380
The study goes on to say
that "food handling gloves

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:34.180
contain replacement plasticizers,

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:36.800
which may be [a] source
of food contamination."

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:38.340
Sounds to me like an easy fix.

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:40.820
Just prepare the food without gloves.

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:45.390
Japan has a ban on DEHP
in food-handling gloves.

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:47.590
Good-er news, if you're
a fan of "Food Wars"

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:50.150
and saw the US versus UK Domino's episode,

00:21:50.150 --> 00:21:54.170
we highlighted BHA and
BHT in the US pepperoni.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:57.810
Well, on the stewardship
page on Domino's website,

00:21:57.810 --> 00:21:59.526
they have stated, ahem,

00:21:59.526 --> 00:22:00.792
"We have eliminated a long list

00:22:00.792 --> 00:22:02.440
of ingredients from all
of our core products

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:06.350
including BHA and BHT and PHOs,

00:22:06.350 --> 00:22:09.490
as well as trans-fat from
core pizza products,"

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:11.140
which is fantastic news.

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:13.050
I clearly was going to eat it anyway,

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.887
but thank you regardless.

00:22:14.887 --> 00:22:16.940
[cricket chirping]
Our cricket is back.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.440
Nothing can stop the mating call

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:21.600
of the North American, or
the West Coast cricket.

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:22.703
OK, here we go. [clears throat]

